# Calc previews

## The chain
  {:label: sec-chain}

The squared distance is a sum of terms, one for each density, and we bound it below.

:calc: {:label: eq-chain}

  :step: $\|F(x)-F(y)\|^2 \ \ge\ c_0\sum_{j=1}^{k}a_j^2$

    :p: Each term is at least $c_0a_j^2$ and the others are nonnegative. ::

  ::

  :step: $\ge\ \frac{c_0}{k}\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{k}a_j\Big)^2$

    :p: By Cauchy-Schwarz. ::

  ::

  :step: $\ge\ \frac{c_0}{4L}\,d(x,y)^2 .$

    :p: Because $\sum_{j=1}^{k} a_j \ge d(x,y)/2$. ::

  ::

::

## Using it
  {:label: sec-use}

Since the pair was arbitrary, :ref:eq-chain:: holds for all pairs.
